==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{recons|čьto|lang=sla-pro}} < {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{recons|kʷid|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|kʷis|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-что.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|[ʂto]|lang=ru}}

===Conjunction===
'''что''' (što) ''(invariable)''

# [[that]]
#:* {{lang|ru|[[я#Russian|Я]] [[думать|думаю]], что [[он]] [[дома|до́ма]]}} — ''I think (that) he’s home.''

===Pronoun===
'''что''' (što)

# {{context|interrogative|lang=ru}} [[what]]
#:* {{lang|ru|Что [[этот|э́то]]}}? — ''What is this?''
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он|Он]] [[не]] [[знать|знает]], что [[этот|э́то]] [[значить|значит]]}} — ''He doesn’t know what this means.''
#:* {{l|ru|зачем|заче́м}}? — ''why? (to what end?)''
#:* {{l|ru|отчего|отчего́}}? — ''why? (from what cause?)''
#:* {{l|ru|почему|почему́}}? — ''why? (on what grounds?)''
# {{context|nonstandard|relative|lang=ru}} [[that]], [[which]]
#:* {{lang|ru|[[книга|кни́га]], что [[на]] [[стол|столе́]]}} — ''the book that is on the table''

====Declension====
{{ru-decl-noun-unc
|что́
|[[чего|чего́]]
|[[чему|чему́]]
|что́
|[[чем|че́м]]
|о [[чём]]}}
<small>* Note: Letter "{{l|ru|ч}}" in nominative and accusative "что" is pronounced as /ʂ/, not /t͡ɕ/.</small>
<small>** Note: Letter "{{l|ru|г}}" in genitive and accusative "чего́" is pronounced as /v/, not /g/.</small>

====Usage notes====
* In informal speech, the genitive form {{l|ru|чего}} often replaces the accusative and sometimes the nominative.

====Synonyms====
* [[чё]] or [[чо]] (čo) (''interrogative pronoun only, non-standard, highly colloquial but common, not used in writing'')
*: Ну чё, пошли что ли? — ''Well, let's go!''
*: Чё он хочет от меня? — ''What (the hell) does he want from me?''
* [[шо]] (šo) (''same as above, used in the South of European Russia or by Russian speakers in Ukraine'')
* [[который]] {{qualifier|standard relative pronoun}}

